{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Indeed, You who love the peoples.</b> And even though You love the peoples, as You said: וִהְיִיתֶם לִי סְגֻלָּה מִכָּל הָעַמִּים (Exodus 19:5), and through this You made known that the entire human species is beloved to You, as the Sages of blessed memory said (Avot 3:18): חָבִיב אָדָם שֶׁנִּבְרָא בְּצֶלֶם — nevertheless, כָּל קְדֹשָׁיו בְּיָדֶךָ (Deuteronomy 33:3). For You said that all His holy ones, of the holiness of fiery law, are in Your hand like a bundle of silver — they are more beloved than the rest of the species, as it says: וְאַתֶּם תִּהְיוּ לִי מַמְלֶכֶת כֹּהֲנִים וְגוֹי קָדוֹשׁ (Exodus 19:6), as the Sages of blessed memory said (Avot 3:18): חֲבִיבִין יִשְׂרָאֵל שֶׁנִּקְרְאוּ בָנִים לַמָּקוֹם." "<b>And they are tukku.</b> Broken, as in וְאִיש תַּכְכִּים הִתְפַּלְלוּ (Proverbs 29:13), with a broken spirit." "<b>At Your feet.</b> At the footstool of Your feet at Sinai."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:32.294563375Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}